1
00:00:00,699 --> 00:00:03,465
Thank God, His people keep growing.

2
00:00:03,465 --> 00:00:06,790
Every Sunday, more families fill the church.

3
00:00:06,790 --> 00:00:10,952
But with so many faces, it becomes almost impossible to know

4
00:00:10,952 --> 00:00:15,820
who came, who is missing, and who quietly drifted away.

5
00:00:16,516 --> 00:00:18,205
Paper lists get lost.

6
00:00:18,205 --> 00:00:21,064
And the people who need a call the most are the easiest to

7
00:00:21,064 --> 00:00:22,049
miss.

8
00:00:22,743 --> 00:00:24,711
That's where Amoinee comes in.

9
00:00:24,711 --> 00:00:28,368
Amoinee, from the Coptic word for "Come!",

10
00:00:28,368 --> 00:00:31,014
helps every church know its people,

11
00:00:31,014 --> 00:00:32,664
and never lose one of them.

12
00:00:33,406 --> 00:00:36,225
For members, it starts with one simple step,

13
00:00:36,225 --> 00:00:37,928
done only once.

14
00:00:37,928 --> 00:00:41,797
Create your profile with your name and contact details,

15
00:00:41,797 --> 00:00:44,178
and choose whether to turn on face check-in.

16
00:00:44,178 --> 00:00:47,423
It's always your choice, and you can turn it off anytime.

17
00:00:48,100 --> 00:00:51,318
At the church door stands the Amoinee kiosk.

18
00:00:51,318 --> 00:00:53,286
Just look at the screen as you walk in.

19
00:00:53,286 --> 00:00:55,587
In a second it welcomes you by name,

20
00:00:55,587 --> 00:00:57,157
and records that you're here.

21
00:00:57,833 --> 00:00:59,682
Prefer not to use your face?

22
00:00:59,682 --> 00:01:00,772
No problem.

23
00:01:00,772 --> 00:01:03,791
Scan the QR code on the kiosk with your phone,

24
00:01:03,791 --> 00:01:06,011
or type the three-digit code of the day.

25
00:01:06,011 --> 00:01:08,659
Nobody is ever left at the door.

26
00:01:09,433 --> 00:01:14,247
For Abouna and church servants, Amoinee turns attendance into

27
00:01:14,247 --> 00:01:15,099
care.

28
00:01:15,796 --> 00:01:18,389
The Today screen shows who is here,

29
00:01:18,389 --> 00:01:22,791
live, as the Liturgy begins, with every arrival time.

30
00:01:22,791 --> 00:01:25,530
Weekly events open check-in on their own,

31
00:01:25,530 --> 00:01:27,340
so no one has to remember.

32
00:01:28,050 --> 00:01:31,454
The Members page keeps every person in one place,

33
00:01:31,454 --> 00:01:35,270
with their photo, consent status, and private notes that only

34
00:01:35,270 --> 00:01:37,253
the church's admins can see.

35
00:01:37,920 --> 00:01:41,909
And the Attendance Sheet gives Abouna a clear summary.

36
00:01:41,909 --> 00:01:46,351
How many came, who is faithful, who is drifting,

37
00:01:46,351 --> 00:01:49,888
and who hasn't come in weeks, ranked from most to least.

38
00:01:49,888 --> 00:01:54,755
A beautiful register shows every person at every service,

39
00:01:54,755 --> 00:01:55,939
at a glance.

40
00:02:07,533 --> 00:02:09,993
When someone misses several Sundays,

41
00:02:09,993 --> 00:02:14,647
Amoinee gently marks them "Follow up needed." Servants add

42
00:02:14,647 --> 00:02:18,225
labels like "Called," "Visited," "Needs prayer," or

43
00:02:18,225 --> 00:02:21,150
"Traveling," and can snooze a reminder when it's not the

44
00:02:21,150 --> 00:02:22,254
right time.

45
00:02:22,254 --> 00:02:26,017
Abouna also sees who came back, who is new,

46
00:02:26,017 --> 00:02:28,385
and whose birthday is this week.

47
00:02:29,076 --> 00:02:32,946
With one tap, Abouna can print a one-page report,

48
00:02:32,946 --> 00:02:35,393
or export everything to Excel.

49
00:02:35,393 --> 00:02:38,279
Each church sees only its own people,

50
00:02:38,279 --> 00:02:40,938
with access given church by church,

51
00:02:40,938 --> 00:02:44,330
and privacy and consent built in from the start.

52
00:02:45,036 --> 00:02:49,305
Because every soul matters, and no one should be forgotten.

53
00:02:49,305 --> 00:02:50,276
Amoinee.

54
00:02:50,276 --> 00:02:51,660
Come, let us worship.

